# Build context allow-list (SPEC decision 68): everything is excluded except the paths that hold
# the compile-time inputs of the nage binary (crates/ brings the crates' tests along), so target/
# (gigabytes), data/ (a live database), fixtures/, the documents and .github/ never reach the
# daemon, and a new input is added here on purpose.
# rust-toolchain.toml stays out: the builder image's own toolchain is the pinned one (the FROM
# tag must equal its channel; scripts/docker-smoke.sh checks that).
*
!Cargo.toml
!Cargo.lock
!.cargo/
!.env
!.sqlx/
!crates/
!migrations/
